From f2c0a6c88d1751080f8113688e275a5fa8b4104a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:48:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(colosseum): drive wall-clock timers from a per-arena
 manual clock

The grace, wall-clock limit and boss time-out GameTests used the real wall
clock, so the 1,500 ms grace raced server tick speed and failed under suite
load. Those tests now install a forward-only ManualClock on their own arena
controller and move time explicitly; every other test keeps the wall clock.

- grace test: same 1,500 ms grace and intent; return at +1,499 ms resumes,
  staying away expires exactly at the deadline
- new: return at exactly +1,500 ms expires (now >= deadline) while a second
  arena's clock is untouched; restore does not inherit the test clock
- new: return at +1,501 ms expires
- limit/boss time-out: expire after an explicit 1 ms step, not host time
- Arena.cleanup releases the clock; assertOwnClock detects a replaced controller

No production code, grace value or assertion intent changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
